<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Morini</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 55 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Coastal people of the Pas-de-Calais, called by Virgil the farthest of men, from whose harbour Caesar sailed to invade Britain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Morini, whose name means people of the sea, lived along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">Channel</a> coast from the Somme to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>, in a land of dunes, marshes and forest. They joined the Belgic coalition of 57 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived by farming, herding and salt-making, and took refuge in forests and marshes rather than defending oppida. Their coast was the shortest crossing to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Caesar campaigned against them in 56 and 55 BCE and sailed for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portus-itius">Portus Itius</a> in their land, probably <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-boulogne">Boulogne</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/therouanne">Tarvenna</a> (Thérouanne), while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Gesoriacum</a> (Boulogne) became the base of the Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">Channel</a> fleet.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/morini.jpg" alt="Morini" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: User:Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 55 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=morini" aria-label="Morini on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4746 511 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Morini lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5066 767h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5066 767h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=morini">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

